#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:33
msgid ""
"Bulbasaur can be seen napping in bright\n"
"sunlight. There is a seed on its back.\n"
"By soaking up the sun's rays, the seed\n"
"grows progressively larger."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:104
msgid ""
"To support its bulb, Ivysaur's legs\n"
"grow sturdy. If it spends more time lying in\n"
"the sunlight, the bud will soon bloom into\n"
"a large flower."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:181
msgid ""
"Venusaur's flower is said to take on vivid\n"
"colors if it gets plenty of nutrition and\n"
"sunlight. The flower's aroma soothes the\n"
"emotions of people."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:269
msgid ""
"In order to support its flower, which\n"
"has grown larger due to Mega Evolution,\n"
"its back and legs have become stronger."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:342
msgid ""
"Spits big amounts of pollen like a volcano.\n"
"Breathing too much of it causes fainting.\n"
"In battle, it swings around two thick vines\n"
"that can easily topple 10-story buildings."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:402
msgid ""
"The flame that burns at the tip of its\n"
"tail is an indication of its emotions.\n"
"The flame wavers when Charmander is\n"
"happy, and blazes when it is enraged."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:472
msgid ""
"Without pity, its sharp claws destroy foes.\n"
"If it encounters a strong enemy, it\n"
"becomes agitated, and the flame on its\n"
"tail flares with a bluish white color."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:550
msgid ""
"A Charizard flies about in search of\n"
"strong opponents. It breathes intense\n"
"flames that can melt any material. However,\n"
"it will never torch a weaker foe."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:623
msgid ""
"The overwhelming power that fills its\n"
"entire body causes it to turn black\n"
"and creates intense blue flames."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:697
msgid ""
"Its bond with its Trainer is the source\n"
"of its power. It boasts speed and\n"
"maneuverability greater than that of a\n"
"jet fighter."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:770
msgid ""
"The flame inside its body burns\n"
"hotter than 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit.\n"
"When Charizard roars, that\n"
"temperature climbs even higher."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:830
msgid ""
"Its shell is not just for protection.\n"
"Its rounded shape and the grooves on its\n"
"surface minimize resistance in water,\n"
"enabling Squirtle to swim at high speeds."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:901
msgid ""
"Its large tail is covered with rich, thick\n"
"fur that deepens in color with age.\n"
"The scratches on its shell are evidence\n"
"of this Pokémon's toughness in battle."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:979
msgid ""
"The waterspouts that protrude from its\n"
"shell are highly accurate. Their bullets of\n"
"water can precisely nail tin cans from\n"
"a distance of over 160 feet."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1055
msgid ""
"The cannon on its back is as powerful\n"
"as a tank gun. Its tough legs and back\n"
"enable it to withstand the recoil from\n"
"firing the cannon."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1128
msgid ""
"It's not very good at precision\n"
"shooting. When attacking, it just fires\n"
"its 31 cannons over and over and\n"
"over."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1188
msgid ""
"Its voracious appetite compels it to\n"
"devour leaves bigger than itself without\n"
"hesitation. It releases a terribly strong\n"
"odor from its antennae."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1262
msgid ""
"Its shell is as hard as an iron slab.\n"
"A Metapod does not move very much\n"
"because it is preparing its soft innards\n"
"for evolution inside the shell."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1342
msgid ""
"It has a superior ability to search for\n"
"delicious honey from flowers. It can seek,\n"
"extract, and carry honey from flowers\n"
"blooming over six miles away."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1438
msgid ""
"Once it has opponents trapped in a\n"
"tornado that could blow away a 10-\n"
"ton truck, it finishes them off with\n"
"its poisonous scales."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1499
msgid ""
"A Weedle has an extremely acute sense\n"
"of smell. It distinguishes its favorite\n"
"kinds of leaves from those it dislikes by\n"
"sniffing with its big red nose."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1573
msgid ""
"It remains virtually immobile while it\n"
"clings to a tree. However, on the inside,\n"
"it busily prepares for evolution. This is\n"
"evident from how hot its shell becomes."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1661
msgid ""
"A Beedrill is extremely territorial.\n"
"For safety reasons, no one should ever\n"
"approach its nest. If angered, they will\n"
"attack in a swarm."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1742
msgid ""
"Its legs have become poison stingers.\n"
"It stabs its prey repeatedly with the\n"
"stingers on its limbs, dealing the final\n"
"blow with the stinger on its rear."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1826
msgid ""
"It has an extremely sharp sense of\n"
"direction. It can unerringly return home to\n"
"its nest, however far it may be removed\n"
"from its familiar surroundings."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1901
msgid ""
"This Pokémon flies around, patrolling its\n"
"large territory. If its living space is\n"
"violated, it shows no mercy in thoroughly\n"
"punishing the foe with its sharp claws."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:1984
msgid ""
"This Pokémon has gorgeous, glossy\n"
"feathers. Many Trainers are so captivated\n"
"by the beautiful feathers on its head that\n"
"they choose Pidgeot as their Pokémon."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:2058
msgid ""
"With its muscular strength now greatly\n"
"increased, it can fly continuously\n"
"for two weeks without resting."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:2135
msgid ""
"A Rattata is cautious in the extreme.\n"
"Even while it is asleep, it constantly\n"
"moves its ears and listens for danger.\n"
"It will make its nest anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:2219
msgid ""
"A Raticate's sturdy fangs grow steadily.\n"
"To keep them ground down, it gnaws on\n"
"rocks and logs. It may even chew on the\n"
"walls of houses."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:2311
msgid ""
"With its incisors, it gnaws through doors\n"
"and infiltrates people's homes.\n"
"Then, with a twitch of its whiskers,\n"
"it steals whatever food it finds."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:2523
msgid ""
"Its loud cry can be heard over half a mile\n"
"away. If its high, keening cry is heard\n"
"echoing all around, it is a sign that they\n"
"are warning each other of danger."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:2595
msgid ""
"Its long neck and elongated beak are\n"
"ideal for catching prey in soil or water.\n"
"It deftly moves this extended and skinny\n"
"beak to pluck prey."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:2671
msgid ""
"An Ekans curls itself up in a spiral while\n"
"it rests. This position allows it to quickly\n"
"respond to an enemy from any direction\n"
"with a threat from its upraised head."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:2750
msgid ""
"This Pokémon has a terrifically strong\n"
"constricting power. It can even flatten\n"
"steel oil drums. Once it wraps its body\n"
"around its foe, escaping is impossible."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3434
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\n"
"is proof of the strong bond Pikachu and\n"
"its partner formed during adventures\n"
"across many different regions."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3499
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\n"
"is proof of the strong bond Pikachu and\n"
"its partner formed during adventures\n"
"across the Hoenn region together."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3564
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\n"
"is proof of the strong bond Pikachu and\n"
"its partner formed during adventures\n"
"across the Sinnoh region together."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3629
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\n"
"is proof of the strong bond Pikachu and\n"
"its partner formed during adventures\n"
"across the Unova region together."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3694
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\n"
"is proof of the strong bond Pikachu and\n"
"its partner formed during adventures\n"
"across the Kalos region together."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3759
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\n"
"is proof of the strong bond Pikachu and\n"
"its partner formed during adventures\n"
"across the Alola region together."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3825
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\n"
"is proof of the strong bond Pikachu and\n"
"its partner formed as the two overcame\n"
"many hardships together."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3890
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\n"
"is proof of the strong bond Pikachu and\n"
"its partner formed during adventures\n"
"across the world together."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:3949
msgid ""
"When it smashes its opponents with\n"
"its bolt-shaped tail, it delivers a\n"
"surge of electricity equivalent to a\n"
"lightning strike."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4096
msgid ""
"If it stores too much electricity, its\n"
"behavior turns aggressive. To avoid this,\n"
"it occasionally discharges excess energy\n"
"and calms itself down."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4179
msgid ""
"It uses psychokinesis to control\n"
"electricity. It focuses psychic energy\n"
"into its tail and rides it like it's surfing.\n"
"Another name for this Pokémon is 'hodad'."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4257
msgid ""
"It resembles an X as it flies through\n"
"the air with 50 million volts of\n"
"electricity sparking from its ears and\n"
"forked tail."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4317
msgid ""
"It fires bolts of electricity from the\n"
"tip of its tail and from the spiky tufts\n"
"of fur growing out of its temples. This\n"
"electricity forms the letter Y."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4374
msgid ""
"When it curls up in a ball, it can make any\n"
"attack bounce off harmlessly. Its hide has\n"
"turned tough and solid as a result of\n"
"living in the desert."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4447
msgid ""
"It curls up in a ball to protect itself from\n"
"enemy attacks. It also curls up to prevent\n"
"heatstroke during the daytime when\n"
"temperatures rise sharply."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4519
msgid ""
"Life on mountains covered with deep snow\n"
"has granted this Pokémon a body of ice\n"
"that's as hard as steel.\n"
"Predators go after its soft belly."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4591
msgid ""
"It uses large, hooked claws to cut a path\n"
"through deep snow as it runs.\n"
"On snowy mountains, this Sandslash\n"
"is faster than any other Pokémon."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4669
msgid ""
"Its highly toxic barbs are thought to have\n"
"developed as protection for this small-\n"
"bodied Pokémon. When enraged, it releases\n"
"a horrible toxin from its horn."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4749
msgid ""
"When it is with its friends or\n"
"family, its barbs are tucked away to\n"
"prevent injury. It appears to become\n"
"nervous if separated from the others."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4828
msgid ""
"It is adept at sending foes flying with\n"
"harsh tackles using its tough, scaly body.\n"
"This Pokémon is at its strongest when\n"
"it is defending its young."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4898
msgid ""
"The male Nidoran has developed muscles\n"
"that freely move its ears in any direction.\n"
"Even the slightest sound does not escape\n"
"this Pokémon's notice."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4971
msgid ""
"Its horn is harder than a diamond.\n"
"If it senses a hostile presence, all the\n"
"barbs on its back bristle up at once, and it\n"
"challenges the foe with all its might."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5051
msgid ""
"A Nidoking's thick tail packs enormously\n"
"destructive power capable of toppling\n"
"a metal transmission tower. Once it goes\n"
"on a rampage, there is no stopping it."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5135
msgid ""
"On nights with many shooting stars,\n"
"Cleffa can be seen dancing in a ring.\n"
"They dance until daybreak, when they\n"
"quench their thirst with the morning dew."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5212
msgid ""
"On every night of a full moon, they come\n"
"out to play. When dawn arrives, the tired\n"
"Clefairy go to sleep nestled up against\n"
"each other in deep and quiet mountains."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5294
msgid ""
"A Clefable uses its wings to skip lightly \n"
"as if it were flying. Its bouncy step\n"
"lets it even walk on water. On quiet,\n"
"moonlit nights, it strolls on lakes."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5369
msgid ""
"It flies by using the power of\n"
"moonlight to control gravity within\n"
"a radius of over 32 feet around it."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5426
msgid ""
"It can freely control fire, making fiery\n"
"orbs fly like will-o'-the-wisps. Just\n"
"before evolution, its six tails grow hot \n"
"as if on fire."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5500
msgid ""
"It has long been said that each of the\n"
"nine tails embody an enchanted power.\n"
"A long-lived Ninetales will have fur that\n"
"shines like gold."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5572
msgid ""
"They live together in a skulk, helping\n"
"one another. In hot weather, this Pokémon\n"
"makes ice shards with its six tails and\n"
"sprays them around to cool itself off."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5645
msgid ""
"While it will guide travelers who get lost\n"
"on a snowy mountain down to the\n"
"mountain's base, it won't forgive anyone\n"
"who harms nature."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5729
msgid ""
"Its soft and pliable body is very bouncy.\n"
"When it sings continuously with all its\n"
"might, its body steadily turns a deepening\n"
"pink color."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5807
msgid ""
"Nothing can avoid falling asleep hearing a\n"
"Jigglypuff's song. The sound waves of its\n"
"singing voice match the brain waves of\n"
"someone in a deep sleep."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5899
msgid ""
"Its fur is the ultimate in luxuriousness.\n"
"Sleeping alongside a Wigglytuff is simply\n"
"divine. Its body expands seemingly without\n"
"end when it inhales."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5970
msgid ""
"While living in pitch-black caverns, their\n"
"eyes gradually grew shut and deprived\n"
"them of vision. They use ultrasonic waves\n"
"to detect obstacles."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6063
msgid ""
"Its fangs easily puncture even thick\n"
"animal hide. It loves to feast on the blood\n"
"of people and Pokémon. It flits about in\n"
"darkness and strikes from behind."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6170
msgid ""
"Over the course of evolution, its hind legs\n"
"turned into wings. By alternately resting\n"
"its front and rear wings, it can fly all day\n"
"without having to stop."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6256
msgid ""
"This Pokémon grows by absorbing moonlight.\n"
"During the daytime, it buries itself in the\n"
"ground, leaving only its leaves exposed to\n"
"avoid detection by its enemies."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6331
msgid ""
"A horribly noxious honey drools from its\n"
"mouth. One whiff of the honey can result\n"
"in memory loss. Some fans are said to\n"
"enjoy this overwhelming stink, however."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6426
msgid ""
"In seasons when it produces more pollen,\n"
"the air around a Vileplume turns yellow\n"
"with the powder as it walks. The pollen is\n"
"highly toxic and causes paralysis."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6515
msgid ""
"Its flower petals deepen in color through\n"
"exposure to sunlight. When cloudy weather\n"
"persists, it does a dance that is thought\n"
"to be a ritual for summoning the sun."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6604
msgid ""
"A Paras has parasitic tochukaso\n"
"mushrooms growing on its back. They grow\n"
"by drawing nutrients from the host. They\n"
"are valued as a medicine for long life."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6694
msgid ""
"Parasect are known to infest the roots of\n"
"large trees en masse and drain nutrients.\n"
"When an infested tree dies, they move\n"
"onto another tree all at once."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6771
msgid ""
"Its coat of thin, stiff hair that covers\n"
"its entire body is said to have evolved\n"
"for protection. Its large eyes never fail\n"
"to spot even miniscule prey."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6850
msgid ""
"Venomoth are nocturnal--they are only\n"
"active at night. Their favorite prey are\n"
"insects that gather around streetlights,\n"
"attracted by the light in the darkness."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6940
msgid ""
"Diglett are raised in most farms.\n"
"The reason is simple--wherever they\n"
"burrow, the soil is left perfectly tilled\n"
"for growing delicious crops."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7019
msgid ""
"Because the triplets originally split from\n"
"one body, they think exactly alike.\n"
"They work cooperatively to burrow\n"
"endlessly through the ground."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7098
msgid ""
"The metal-rich geology of its habitat\n"
"caused it to develop steel whiskers on its\n"
"head that change shape depending on its\n"
"mood and when communicating with others."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7173
msgid ""
"Their beautiful, metallic whiskers create\n"
"a sort of protective helmet on\n"
"heir heads, and they also function\n"
"as highly precise sensors."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7261
msgid ""
"Meowth withdraw their sharp claws into\n"
"their paws to silently sneak about.\n"
"For some reason, this Pokémon loves\n"
"shiny coins that glitter with light."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7341
msgid ""
"A Persian's six bold whiskers sense air\n"
"movements to determine what is in its\n"
"vicinity. It becomes docile if grabbed\n"
"by the whiskers."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7411
msgid ""
"It's accustomed to luxury because it used\n"
"to live with Alolan royalty. Highly smart\n"
"and proud, it's famously difficult to\n"
"handle, but that also makes it popular."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7483
msgid ""
"It looks down on everyone other than\n"
"itself. In contrast to its lovely face, it\n"
"is so brutal that it tortures its weakened\n"
"prey rather than finishing them off."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7553
msgid ""
"Living with a savage, seafaring people has\n"
"hardened its body so much that parts of it\n"
"turned to iron. Darker coins are harder\n"
"and garner more respect among Meowth."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7620
msgid ""
"What appears to be an iron helmet is\n"
"actually hardened hair. This Pokémon\n"
"lives for the thrill of battle."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7685
msgid ""
"The pattern that has appeared on\n"
"its giant coin is thought to be the\n"
"key to unlocking the secrets of the\n"
"Dynamax phenomenon."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7746
msgid ""
"When its headache intensifies, it starts\n"
"using strange powers. However, it has no\n"
"recollection of its powers, so it always\n"
"looks befuddled and bewildered."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7817
msgid ""
"A Golduck is an adept swimmer.\n"
"It sometimes joins competitive swimmers\n"
"in training. It uses psychic powers when\n"
"its forehead shimmers with light."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7892
msgid ""
"When it starts shaking and its nasal\n"
"breathing turns rough, it's a sure sign\n"
"of anger. However, since this happens\n"
"instantly, there is no time to flee."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7970
msgid ""
"When it becomes furious, its blood\n"
"circulation becomes more robust, and\n"
"its muscles are made stronger. But it\n"
"also becomes much less intelligent."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8046
msgid ""
"When its anger rose beyond a\n"
"critical point, this Pokémon gained power\n"
"that is unfettered by the limits of\n"
"its physical body."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8112
msgid ""
"Its superb sense of smell ensures that\n"
"this Pokémon won't forget any scent,\n"
"no matter what. It uses its sense of smell\n"
"to detect the emotions of others."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8186
msgid ""
"This fleet-footed Pokémon is said to run\n"
"over 6,200 miles in a single day and night.\n"
"The fire that blazes wildly within its body\n"
"is its source of power."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8255
msgid ""
"They patrol their territory in pairs.\n"
"It's believed the igneous rock components\n"
"in the fur of this species are the result\n"
"of volcanic activity in its habitat."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8322
msgid ""
"Snaps at its foes with fangs cloaked in\n"
"blazing flame. Despite its bulk, it deftly\n"
"feints every which way, leading opponents\n"
"on a deceptively merry chase."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8391
msgid ""
"It is possible to see this Pokémon's spiral\n"
"innards right through its thin skin.\n"
"However, the skin is also very flexible.\n"
"Even sharp fangs bounce right off it."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8462
msgid ""
"Its body surface is always wet and slick\n"
"with an oily fluid. Because of this greasy\n"
"covering, it can easily slip and slide out\n"
"of the clutches of any enemy in battle."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8548
msgid ""
"Its highly developed muscles never grow\n"
"fatigued, however much it exercises.\n"
"This Pokémon can swim back and forth\n"
"across the Pacific Ocean without effort."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8623
msgid ""
"The curled hair on its head proves its\n"
"status as a king. It is said that the\n"
"longer and curlier the hair, the more\n"
"respect it earns from its peers."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8717
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that sleeps 18 hours a day.\n"
"Observation revealed that it uses\n"
"Teleport to change its location once\n"
"every hour."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8790
msgid ""
"It is rumored that a boy with psychic\n"
"abilities suddenly transformed into\n"
"Kadabra while he was assisting research\n"
"into extrasensory powers."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8889
msgid ""
"While it has strong psychic abilities and\n"
"high intelligence, an Alakazam's muscles\n"
"are very weak. It uses psychic power to\n"
"move its body."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8983
msgid ""
"Having traded away its muscles, Alakazam's\n"
"true power has been unleashed. With its\n"
"psychic powers, it can foresee all things."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9070
msgid ""
"It continually undertakes strenuous\n"
"training to master all forms of martial\n"
"arts. Its strength lets it easily hoist\n"
"a sumo wrestler onto its shoulders."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9147
msgid ""
"A belt is worn by a Machoke to keep its\n"
"overwhelming power under control.\n"
"Because it is so dangerous, no one has\n"
"ever removed the belt."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9229
msgid ""
"It is impossible to defend against punches\n"
"and chops doled out by its four arms.\n"
"Its fighting spirit flares up when it faces\n"
"a tough opponent."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9308
msgid ""
"One of these Pokémon once used\n"
"its immeasurable strength to lift a\n"
"large ship that was in trouble. It\n"
"then carried the ship to port."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9368
msgid ""
"A Bellsprout's thin and flexible body lets\n"
"it bend and sway to avoid any attack,\n"
"however strong it may be. From its mouth,\n"
"it leaks a fluid that melts even iron."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9438
msgid ""
"At night, a Weepinbell hangs on to a tree\n"
"branch with its hooked rear and sleeps.\n"
"If it moves around in its sleep, it may\n"
"wake up to find itself on the ground."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9528
msgid ""
"The long vine extending from its head is\n"
"waved about as if it were a living thing to\n"
"attract prey. When an unsuspecting victim\n"
"approaches, it is swallowed whole."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9607
msgid ""
"The volume of this Pokémon's acid\n"
"has increased due to Mega Evolution,\n"
"filling its mouth. If not careful,\n"
"the acid will overflow and spill out."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9664
msgid ""
"Its body is almost entirely composed of\n"
"water. It ensnares its foe with its two\n"
"long tentacles, then stabs with the poison\n"
"stingers at their tips."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9736
msgid ""
"It lives in complex rock formations on\n"
"the ocean floor and traps prey using its\n"
"80 tentacles. Its red orbs glow when it\n"
"grows excited or agitated."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9814
msgid ""
"It climbs mountain paths using only the\n"
"power of its arms. Because they look just\n"
"like boulders lining paths, hikers may step\n"
"on them without noticing."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9886
msgid ""
"They descend from mountains by tumbling\n"
"down steep slopes. They are so brutal,\n"
"they smash aside obstructing trees and\n"
"massive boulders with thunderous tackles."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9967
msgid ""
"It is said to live in volcanic craters\n"
"on mountain peaks. Once a year, it sheds\n"
"its hide and grows larger. The shed hide\n"
"crumbles and returns to the soil."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10039
msgid ""
"Its body is a magnetic stone. Iron sand\n"
"attach to parts of its body with stronger\n"
"magnetism. If you carelessly step on one,\n"
"it will headbutt and shock you in anger."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10112
msgid ""
"When two Graveler smash each other over\n"
"dravite, their favorite food, they cause\n"
"flashes of light and booming noises.\n"
"People call them “fireworks of the earth.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10186
msgid ""
"It fires rocks charged with electricity.\n"
"Even if the rock isn't fired that\n"
"accurately, just grazing an opponent\n"
"will cause numbness and fainting."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10258
msgid ""
"A Ponyta is very weak at birth. It can\n"
"barely stand up. Its legs become stronger\n"
"as it stumbles and falls while trying to\n"
"keep up with its parent."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10328
msgid ""
"It usually canters casually in the fields\n"
"and plains. But once a Rapidash turns\n"
"serious, its fiery manes flare and blaze\n"
"as it gallops its way up to 150 mph."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10397
msgid ""
"Its small horn hides a healing power.\n"
"This Pokémon will look into your eyes and\n"
"read the contents of your heart. If it\n"
"finds evil there, it promptly hides away."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10464
msgid ""
"Little can stand up to its psycho cut.\n"
"Unleashed from this Pokémon's horn,\n"
"the move will punch a hole right\n"
"through a thick metal sheet."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10533
msgid ""
"It catches prey by dipping its tail in\n"
"water at the side of a river. But it often\n"
"forgets what it is doing and spends entire\n"
"days just loafing at water's edge."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10609
msgid ""
"Its tail has a Shellder firmly attached\n"
"with a bite. As a result, the tail can't be\n"
"used for fishing anymore. This forces it\n"
"to reluctantly swim and catch prey."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10679
msgid ""
"It undertakes research every day to\n"
"solve the mysteries of the world.\n"
"However, it apparently forgets everything\n"
"if the Shellder on its head comes off."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10750
msgid ""
"When bathed in the energy of Mega\n"
"Evolution, Shellder converts into\n"
"impregnable armor. There is virtually no\n"
"change in Slowpoke."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10824
msgid ""
"Although it is normally zoned out, its\n"
"expression abruptly sharpens on occasion.\n"
"The cause seems to lie in Slowpoke's diet,\n"
"which also give their tails a spicy flavor."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10897
msgid ""
"A Shellder bite set off a chemical reaction\n"
"with the spices inside Slowbro's body,\n"
"causing Slowbro to become a\n"
"Poison-type Pokémon."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10963
msgid ""
"A combination of toxins and the shock of\n"
"evolving has increased Shellder's\n"
"intelligence to the point that Shellder\n"
"now controls Slowking."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11035
msgid ""
"The units at its sides are extremely\n"
"powerful magnets. They generate enough\n"
"magnetism to draw in iron objects from\n"
"over 300 feet away."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11107
msgid ""
"It is actually three Magnemite linked\n"
"by magnetism. It generates powerful radio\n"
"waves that raise temperatures by 3.6\n"
"degrees F within a 3,300-foot radius."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11191
msgid ""
"As it zooms through the sky, this\n"
"Pokémon seems to be receiving signals\n"
"of unknown origin, while transmitting its\n"
"own signals of unknown purpose."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11272
msgid ""
"It is always seen with a stick from a plant.\n"
"Apparently, there are good sticks and bad\n"
"sticks. This Pokémon occasionally fights\n"
"with others over choice sticks."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11354
msgid ""
"The stalks of leeks are thicker and longer\n"
"in the Galar region. Brave Farfetch'd\n"
"warriors that adapted to these stalks\n"
"took on a unique form."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11423
msgid ""
"Only Farfetch'd that have survived many\n"
"battles can attain this evolution. When\n"
"this Pokémon's leek withers, it will\n"
"retire from combat."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11490
msgid ""
"Even while eating or sleeping, one of the\n"
"heads remains always vigilant for any sign\n"
"of danger. When threatened, it flees at\n"
"over 60 miles per hour."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11583
msgid ""
"A peculiar Pokémon species with three\n"
"heads. It vigorously races across grassy\n"
"plains even in arid seasons with little\n"
"rainfall."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11674
msgid ""
"Seel hunt for prey in frigid, ice-covered\n"
"seas. When it needs to breathe, it punches\n"
"a hole through the ice with the sharply\n"
"protruding section of its head."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11748
msgid ""
"It loves to snooze on bitterly cold ice.\n"
"The sight of this Pokémon sleeping on\n"
"a glacier was mistakenly thought to be\n"
"a mermaid by a mariner long ago."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11818
msgid ""
"Born from polluted sludge in the sea,\n"
"Grimer's favorite food is anything filthy.\n"
"They feed on wastewater pumped out from\n"
"factories."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11892
msgid ""
"It prefers warm and humid habitats.\n"
"In the summertime, the toxic substances\n"
"in its body intensify, making Muk reek like\n"
"putrid kitchen garbage."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11965
msgid ""
"There are a hundred or so of them living\n"
"in Alola's waste-disposal site. They're all\n"
"hard workers who eat a lot of trash. Grimer\n"
"seems to relish any and all kinds of trash."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12038
msgid ""
"While it's unexpectedly quiet and friendly,\n"
"if it's not fed any trash for a while,,\n"
"it will smash its Trainer's furnishings,\n"
"and eat up the fragments."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12116
msgid ""
"At night, it burrows a hole in the seafloor\n"
"with its broad tongue to make a place to\n"
"sleep. While asleep, it closes its shell,\n"
"but leaves its tongue hanging out."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12193
msgid ""
"It swims in the sea by swallowing water,\n"
"then jetting it out toward the rear.\n"
"The Cloyster shoots spikes from its\n"
"shell using the same system."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12263
msgid ""
"When exposed to a strong wind, a Gastly's\n"
"gaseous body quickly dwindles away.\n"
"They cluster under the eaves of houses\n"
"to escape the ravages of wind."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12337
msgid ""
"If a Haunter beckons you while it is\n"
"floating in darkness, don't approach it.\n"
"This Pokémon will try to lick you with its\n"
"tongue and steal your life away."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12426
msgid ""
"Deep in the night, your shadow cast by\n"
"a streetlight may suddenly overtake you.\n"
"It is actually a Gengar running past\n"
"you, pretending to be your shadow."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12500
msgid ""
"Gengar's relationships are warped. It\n"
"tries to take the lives of anyone and\n"
"everyone. It will even try to curse the\n"
"Trainer who is its master!"
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12575
msgid ""
"Rumor has it that its gigantic\n"
"mouth leads not into its body, filled\n"
"with cursed energy, but instead\n"
"directly to the afterlife."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12635
msgid ""
"There is a magnet in its brain that\n"
"prevents an Onix from losing direction\n"
"while tunneling. As it grows older, its body\n"
"becomes steadily rounder and smoother."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12708
msgid ""
"Steelix live even further underground\n"
"than Onix. This Pokémon is known to dig\n"
"toward the earth's core, reaching a depth\n"
"of over six-tenths of a mile underground."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12799
msgid ""
"The cells within its body, crystallized by\n"
"the energy produced from Mega Evolution,\n"
"are stronger than any mineral and able\n"
"to withstand any temperature."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12875
msgid ""
"If your nose becomes itchy while you are\n"
"sleeping, it's a sure sign that a Drowzee is\n"
"standing above your pillow and trying to\n"
"eat your dream through your nostrils."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12952
msgid ""
"The arcing movement and glitter of the\n"
"pendulum in a Hypno's hand lull the foe\n"
"into deep hypnosis. While searching for\n"
"prey, it polishes the pendulum."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13039
msgid ""
"Krabby live in holes dug into beaches.\n"
"On sandy shores with little in the way\n"
"of food, they can be seen squabbling with\n"
"each other over territory."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13112
msgid ""
"It waves its huge, oversized claw in the\n"
"air to communicate with others.\n"
"But since the claw is so heavy, this\n"
"Pokémon quickly tires."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13183
msgid ""
"The flow of Gigantamax energy has\n"
"spurred this Pokémon's left pincer\n"
"to grow to an enormous size. That\n"
"claw can pulverize anything."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13243
msgid ""
"It bears an uncanny and unexplained\n"
"resemblance to a Poké Ball. Because it\n"
"explodes at the slightest shock, even\n"
"veteran Trainers treat it with caution."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13321
msgid ""
"They appear in great numbers at electric\n"
"power plants. Because they feed on\n"
"electricity, they cause massive and\n"
"chaotic blackouts in nearby cities."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13392
msgid ""
"It resembles an ancient Poké Ball design.\n"
"When excited, it discharges the electric\n"
"current it has stored in its belly, then\n"
"lets out a great, uproarious laugh."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13458
msgid ""
"The tissue on the surface of its body is\n"
"similar in composition to an Apricorn.\n"
"When irritated, it lets loose an electric\n"
"current equal to 20 lightning bolts."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13528
msgid ""
"It consists of six eggs that care for each\n"
"other. The eggs attract each other and\n"
"spin around. When cracks increasingly\n"
"appear, it is close to evolution."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13620
msgid ""
"Originally from the tropics, Exeggutor's\n"
"heads grow larger from exposure to strong\n"
"sunlight. It is said that when the heads\n"
"fall, they group to form an Exeggcute."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13689
msgid ""
"Alola is the best environment for\n"
"this Pokémon. Local people take pride\n"
"in its appearance, saying this is how\n"
"Exeggutor ought to look."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13763
msgid ""
"It pines for the mother it will never see\n"
"again. Seeing a likeness of its mother in\n"
"the full moon, it cries. The stains on the\n"
"skull it wears are from its tears."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13843
msgid ""
"A Marowak is the evolved form of a Cubone\n"
"that has grown tough by overcoming the\n"
"grief of losing its mother. Its tempered\n"
"and hardened spirit is not easily broken."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14050
msgid ""
"Tyrogue become stressed out if they do\n"
"not get to train every day. When raising\n"
"this Pokémon, the Trainer must establish\n"
"a regular training schedule."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14125
msgid ""
"Its legs freely stretch and contract.\n"
"Using these springlike limbs, it bowls over\n"
"foes with devastating kicks. After battle,\n"
"it rubs down its tired legs."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14196
msgid ""
"A Hitmonchan is said to possess the\n"
"spirit of a boxer who aimed to become the\n"
"world champion. Having an indomitable\n"
"spirit means that it will never give up."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14276
msgid ""
"Its technique of kicking while spinning is\n"
"a remarkable mix of both offense and\n"
"defense. Hitmontop travel faster\n"
"spinning than they do walking."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14349
msgid ""
"Whenever it sees something unfamiliar,\n"
"it always licks the object because it\n"
"memorizes things by texture and taste.\n"
"It is somewhat put off by sour things."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14421
msgid ""
"The long tongue is always soggy with\n"
"slobber. The saliva contains a solvent\n"
"that causes numbness. Getting too close\n"
"to it will leave you soaked with drool."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14502
msgid ""
"Getting up close to a Koffing will give\n"
"you a chance to observe, through its thin\n"
"skin, the toxic gases swirling inside. It\n"
"blows up at the slightest stimulation."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14584
msgid ""
"By diluting its toxic gases with a special\n"
"process, the highest grade of perfume can\n"
"be extracted. To Weezing, gases emanating\n"
"from garbage are the ultimate feast."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14658
msgid ""
"Long ago, when droves of factories fouled\n"
"the air with pollution, it changed into this\n"
"form for some reason. It consumes air\n"
"pollutant particles, expelling clean air."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14727
msgid ""
"Once it starts running, it doesn't stop.\n"
"Its tiny brain makes it so stupid that it\n"
"can't remember why it started running in\n"
"the first place."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14811
msgid ""
"Its horn, which rotates like a drill,\n"
"destroys tall buildings with one strike.\n"
"It stands on its hind legs, and its brain\n"
"is well developed."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14901
msgid ""
"It can launch a rock held in its hand\n"
"like a missile by tightening and then\n"
"expanding its muscles instantaneously.\n"
"Geodude are shot at rare times."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14988
msgid ""
"It carries a round white rock in its\n"
"belly pouch. If it gets along well with\n"
"someone, it will sometimes give that\n"
"person the rock."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15060
msgid ""
"Chansey lay nutritionally excellent eggs\n"
"every day. The eggs are so delicious, they\n"
"are eagerly devoured by even those people\n"
"who have lost their appetite."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15139
msgid ""
"If it senses sadness with its fluffy fur,\n"
"a Blissey will rush over to the sad person,\n"
"however far away, to share an egg of\n"
"happiness that brings a smile to any face."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15213
msgid ""
"Its vines snap off easily and painlessly\n"
"if they are grabbed, allowing it to make a\n"
"quick getaway. The lost vines are replaced\n"
"by new growth the very next day."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15285
msgid ""
"It ensnares prey by extending arms made\n"
"of vines. Even if one of its arms is eaten,\n"
"it's fine. The Pokémon regenerates quickly\n"
"and will go right back to normal."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15370
msgid ""
"If you come across a young Kangaskhan\n"
"playing by itself, never try to catch it.\n"
"The baby's parent is sure to be in the area,\n"
"and it will become violently enraged."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15446
msgid ""
"When the mother sees the back of her\n"
"Mega-Evolved child, it makes her think\n"
"of the day when her child will inevitably\n"
"leave her."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15526
msgid ""
"By cleverly flicking the fins on its back\n"
"side to side, it moves in any direction\n"
"while facing forward. It spits ink to\n"
"escape if it senses danger."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15603
msgid ""
"The poisonous barbs all over its body are\n"
"highly valued as ingredients for making\n"
"traditional herbal medicine. It shows no\n"
"mercy to anything approaching its nest."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15690
msgid ""
"It sleeps quietly, deep on the seafloor.\n"
"When it comes up to the surface, it\n"
"creates a huge whirlpool that can swallow\n"
"even ships."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15763
msgid ""
"In the springtime, schools of Goldeen\n"
"can be seen swimming up falls and rivers.\n"
"It metes out staggering damage with its\n"
"single horn."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15852
msgid ""
"It punches holes in boulders on stream-\n"
"beds. This is a clever innovation that\n"
"prevents its eggs from being attacked or\n"
"washed away by the current."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15939
msgid ""
"It gathers with others in the night and\n"
"makes its red core glow on and off with\n"
"the twinkling stars. It can regenerate\n"
"limbs if they are severed from its body."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16011
msgid ""
"People in ancient times imagined that\n"
"Starmie were transformed from the\n"
"reflections of stars that twinkled on\n"
"gentle waves at night."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16089
msgid ""
"Its movements have become more\n"
"humanlike. Whether it's simply\n"
"trying to communicate or wants to\n"
"supplant humanity is unclear."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16154
msgid ""
"In an attempt to confuse its enemy,\n"
"it mimics the enemy's movements.\n"
"Once mimicked, the foe cannot take\n"
"its eyes off this Pokémon."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16235
msgid ""
"A Mr. Mime is a master of pantomime. It can\n"
"convince others that something unseeable\n"
"actually exists. Once believed, the\n"
"imaginary object does become real."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16308
msgid ""
"Its talent is tap-dancing. It can radiate\n"
"chilliness from the bottoms of its feet to\n"
"to create a floor of ice, which this\n"
"Pokémon can kick up to use as a barrier."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16376
msgid ""
"It's highly skilled at tap-dancing. It\n"
"waves its cane of ice in time with its\n"
"graceful movements."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16445
msgid ""
"Its blindingly fast speed adds to the\n"
"sharpness of its twin forearm scythes.\n"
"The scythes can slice through thick logs\n"
"in one wicked stroke."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16549
msgid ""
"A Scizor has a body with the hardness of\n"
"steel. It is not easily fazed by ordinary\n"
"sorts of attacks. It flaps its wings to\n"
"regulate its body temperature."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16634
msgid ""
"The excess energy that bathes this\n"
"Pokémon keeps it in constant danger of\n"
"overflow. It can't sustain a battle over\n"
"long periods of time."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16705
msgid ""
"A violent creature that fells trees with\n"
"its crude axes and shields itself with hard\n"
"stone. Should one encounter this Pokémon\n"
"in the wild, one's only recourse is to flee."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16776
msgid ""
"It actively runs about, but also falls\n"
"often. Whenever it falls, it will check its\n"
"reflection on a lake's surface to make\n"
"sure its face hasn't become dirty."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16850
msgid ""
"A Jynx sashays rhythmically as if it were\n"
"dancing. Its motions are so bouncingly\n"
"alluring, people seeing it are compelled to\n"
"shake their hips without noticing."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16924
msgid ""
"If it touches metal and discharges the\n"
"electricity it has stored in its body, an\n"
"Elekid begins swinging its arms in circles\n"
"to recharge itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16996
msgid ""
"When a storm approaches, it competes with\n"
"others to scale heights that are likely to\n"
"be stricken by lightning. Some towns use\n"
"Electabuzz in place of lightning rods."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17077
msgid ""
"When it gets excited, it thumps its chest.\n"
"With every thud, thunder roars, electric\n"
"sparks shower all around and blue sparks\n"
"begin to crackle between its horns."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17150
msgid ""
"If a Magby is spouting yellow flames from\n"
"its mouth, it is in good health. When it is\n"
"fatigued, black smoke will be mixed in with\n"
"the flames."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17222
msgid ""
"In battle, it blows out intense flames from\n"
"all over its body to intimidate its foe.\n"
"These fiery bursts create heat waves that\n"
"ignite grass and trees in the area."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17301
msgid ""
"According to what is known, a single pair\n"
"of male and female Magmortar lives in\n"
"one volcano. From its arm, it launches\n"
"fireballs hotter than 3,600ºF."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17374
msgid ""
"Their pincers are strong enough to\n"
"shatter thick logs. Because they dislike\n"
"cold, Pinsir burrow and sleep under\n"
"the ground on chilly nights."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17451
msgid ""
"The influence of Mega Evolution leaves it\n"
"in a state of constant excitement.\n"
"It pierces enemies with its two large\n"
"horns before shredding them."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17537
msgid ""
"It is not satisfied unless it is rampaging\n"
"at all times. If there is no opponent for\n"
"Tauros to battle, it will charge at thick\n"
"trees and knock them down to calm itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17608
msgid ""
"This Pokémon has a muscular body\n"
"and excels at close-quarters combat.\n"
"It uses its short horns to strike\n"
"the opponent’s weak spots."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17674
msgid ""
"When heated by fire energy, its horns can\n"
"get hotter than 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit.\n"
"Those gored by them will suffer\n"
"both wounds and burns."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17740
msgid ""
"This Pokémon blasts water from holes on\n"
"the tips of its horns--the high-pressure\n"
"jets pierce right through\n"
"Tauros’s enemies."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17809
msgid ""
"Its swimming muscles are weak, so it is\n"
"easily washed away by currents. In places\n"
"where water pools, you can see many\n"
"Magikarp deposited there by the flow."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17897
msgid ""
"It is an extremely vicious and violent\n"
"Pokémon. When humans begin to fight,\n"
"it will appear and burn everything to the\n"
"ground with intensely hot flames."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17984
msgid ""
"Although it obeys its instinctive drive to\n"
"destroy everything within its reach, it\n"
"will respond to orders from a Trainer it\n"
"truly trusts."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18062
msgid ""
"People have driven Lapras almost to the\n"
"point of extinction. In the evenings,\n"
"it is said to sing plaintively as it seeks\n"
"what few others of its kind still remain."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18134
msgid ""
"Over 5,000 people can ride on its\n"
"shell at once. And it's a very\n"
"comfortable ride, without the slightest\n"
"shaking or swaying."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18197
msgid ""
"A Ditto rearranges its cell structure to\n"
"transform itself. However, if it tries to\n"
"change based on its memory, it will get\n"
"details wrong."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18372
msgid ""
"Having gotten even friendlier and\n"
"more innocent, Eevee tries to play\n"
"with anyone around, only to end up\n"
"crushing them with its immense body."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18507
msgid ""
"Vaporeon underwent a spontaneous\n"
"mutation and grew fins and gills that\n"
"allow them to live underwater. They have\n"
"the ability to freely control water."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18573
msgid ""
"Its cells generate weak power that is\n"
"amplified by its fur's static electricity\n"
"to drop thunderbolts. The bristling fur is\n"
"made of electrically charged needles."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18639
msgid ""
"Flareon's fluffy fur releases heat into\n"
"the air so that its body does not get\n"
"excessively hot. Its body temperature can\n"
"rise to a maximum of 1,650 degrees F."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18706
msgid ""
"An Espeon is extremely loyal to any\n"
"Trainer it considers to be worthy. It is\n"
"said to have developed precognitive\n"
"powers to protect its Trainer from harm."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18773
msgid ""
"Umbreon evolved from exposure to the\n"
"moon's energy pulses. It lurks in darkness\n"
"and waits for its foes to move. The rings\n"
"on its body glow when it leaps to attack."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18841
msgid ""
"Its cellular composition is closer to\n"
"that of a plant than an animal. It uses\n"
"photosynthesis to produce its energy\n"
"supply without eating food."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18908
msgid ""
"It can control its body temperature\n"
"at will. This enables it to freeze the\n"
"moisture in the atmosphere, creating\n"
"flurries of diamond dust."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18978
msgid ""
"Its ribbonlike feelers give off an aura\n"
"that weakens hostility in its prey, causing\n"
"them to let down their guard. A moment\n"
"later, it pounces."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19052
msgid ""
"It is capable of reverting itself entirely\n"
"back to program data in order to enter\n"
"cyberspace. A Porygon is copy-\n"
"protected so it cannot be duplicated."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19129
msgid ""
"It was created by humans using the power\n"
"of science. It has been given artificial\n"
"intelligence that enables it to learn new\n"
"gestures and emotions on its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19210
msgid ""
"In order to create a more advanced\n"
"Pokémon, an additional program was\n"
"installed, but apparently it contained a\n"
"defect that made it move oddly."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19289
msgid ""
"One of the ancient and long-since-extinct\n"
"Pokémon that have been regenerated\n"
"from fossils by humans. If attacked,\n"
"it withdraws into its hard shell."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19363
msgid ""
"An Omastar uses its tentacles to capture\n"
"its prey. It is believed to have become\n"
"extinct because its shell grew too large,\n"
"making its movements slow and ponderous."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19439
msgid ""
"It is a Pokémon that has been regenerated\n"
"from a fossil. However, in rare cases, living\n"
"examples have been discovered. Kabuto\n"
"have not changed for 300 million years."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19519
msgid ""
"Kabutops once swam underwater to hunt \n"
"for prey. It was apparently evolving from\n"
"being a water dweller to living on land as\n"
"evident from changes in its gills and legs."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19589
msgid ""
"Aerodactyl is a Pokémon from the age\n"
"of dinosaurs. It was regenerated from DNA\n"
"extracted from amber. It is imagined to\n"
"have been the king of the skies."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19666
msgid ""
"The power of Mega Evolution has\n"
"completely restored its genes. The rocks\n"
"on its body are harder than diamond."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19744
msgid ""
"When it finds something that looks like\n"
"it might be edible, it goes right ahead\n"
"and swallows it whole. That's why it gets\n"
"fatter day by day."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19816
msgid ""
"Snorlax's typical day consists of nothing\n"
"more than eating and sleeping. It is such\n"
"a docile Pokémon that there are children\n"
"who use its big belly as a place to play."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19889
msgid ""
"Gigantamax energy has affected\n"
"stray seeds and even pebbles that\n"
"got stuck to Snorlax, making them grow\n"
"to a huge size."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19956
msgid ""
"Articuno is a legendary bird Pokémon that\n"
"can control ice. The flapping of its wings\n"
"chills the air. As a result, it is said that\n"
"when this Pokémon flies, snow will fall."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20029
msgid ""
"It fires beams that immobilize opponents\n"
"as if they had been frozen solid.\n"
"Its feather-like blades of psychic energy\n"
"rip through thick iron sheets like paper."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20109
msgid ""
"Zapdos is a legendary bird Pokémon that\n"
"has the ability to control electricity.\n"
"It usually lives in thunderclouds. It gains\n"
"power if it is stricken by lightning bolts."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20182
msgid ""
"When its feathers rub together, they\n"
"produce a crackling sound like the\n"
"zapping of electricity. Apparently, it runs\n"
"through the mountains at over 180 mph."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20258
msgid ""
"Moltres is a legendary bird Pokémon\n"
"that can control fire. If injured, it is said\n"
"to dip its body in the molten magma of\n"
"a volcano to burn and heal itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20359
msgid ""
"This Pokémon's sinister, flame-like aura\n"
"will consume the spirit of any creature\n"
"it hits. Victims become burned-out\n"
"shadows of themselves."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20430
msgid ""
"A Dratini continually molts and sloughs\n"
"off its old skin. It does so because the\n"
"life energy within its body steadily builds\n"
"to reach uncontrollable levels."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20500
msgid ""
"A Dragonair stores an enormous amount of\n"
"energy inside its body. It is said to alter\n"
"the weather around it by loosing energy\n"
"from the crystals on its neck and tail."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20576
msgid ""
"It can circle the globe in just 16 hours.\n"
"It is a kindhearted Pokémon that leads\n"
"lost and foundering ships in a storm\n"
"to the safety of land."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20652
msgid ""
"Mega Evolution has excessively\n"
"powered up this Pokémon's feelings\n"
"of kindness. It finishes off its\n"
"opponents with mercy in its heart."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20715
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that was created by genetic\n"
"manipulation. However, even though the\n"
"scientific power of humans made its body,\n"
"they failed to give it a warm heart."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20791
msgid ""
"Psychic power has augmented its muscles.\n"
"It has a grip strength of one ton and can\n"
"sprint a hundred meters in two seconds\n"
"flat!"
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20870
msgid ""
"Despite its diminished size, its mental\n"
"power has grown phenomenally. With a mere\n"
"thought, it can smash a skyscraper to\n"
"smithereens."
msgstr ""

#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20957
msgid ""
"A Mew is said to possess the genes of all\n"
"Pokémon. It is capable of making itself\n"
"invisible at will, so it entirely avoids\n"
"notice even if it approaches people."
msgstr ""

